# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: banner — print a startup welcome banner unless -q/--quiet
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: cli-feature
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: feature-banner

* Resolution (2026-08-03, clautolisp 1.7.9)

Implemented in =emit-repl-banner= (tools/clautolisp/source/main.lisp). The
plumbing already existed — =-q/--quiet= maps to verbosity :warn, =repl-loop=
gates the banner with =(unless quiet-p ...)= where =quiet-p = (eq verbosity
:warn)= — so only the banner *content* changed: the former one-liner is now
the full welcome:

    Welcome to clautolisp Version 1.7.9
    Copyright 2026-2026 Ogamita Ltd
    Licensed under AGPL; source codes available at:
    http://gitlab.com/ogamita/clautolisp/
    AUTOLISP REPL (STRICT dialect, mock-host host) — Ctrl-D to exit.

Details:
- Version from =*version*=; dialect/host from the live session
  (=autolisp-dialect-name= / =host-name=) so =--clautolisp= shows
  "CLAUTOLISP dialect", =--host null= shows "null-host", etc.
- Copyright end-year is the current year (=(nth-value 5 (get-decoded-time))=)
  against =*copyright-start-year*= = 2026, so a new year needs no source edit.
- =-q/--quiet= suppresses the whole banner; =-v/--verbose= still appends the
  non-default-knobs line (mock-input/gui/trace/debug) after it.
- Updated the demo transcript documentation/demo/clautolisp-1-aldo-sedit.txt.

Verified by running the built image: default prints the 5-line banner + =_$=
prompt, =-q= prints only =_$=, =--clautolisp -v= shows the CLAUTOLISP dialect.
Full SBCL suite green.

* Original request

Unless -q|--quiet is given, print a banner formatted as such:

    Welcome to clautolisp Version 9.9.9
    Copyright 2026-2026 Ogamita Ltd
    Licensed under AGPL; source codes available at:
    http://gitlab.com/ogamita/clautolisp/
    AUTOLISP REPL (STRICT dialect, mock-host host) — Ctrl-D to exit.

    _$
